From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpc823 <11076149+mpc823@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:12:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rcinput: support time64 input_event layout

Linux input headers use the time64-compatible seconds and microseconds
fields when _TIME_BITS=64 is enabled on 32-bit targets.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: mpc823 <11076149+mpc823@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/driver/rcinput.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/driver/rcinput.cpp b/src/driver/rcinput.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/driver/rcinput.cpp
+++ b/src/driver/rcinput.cpp
@@ -1338,1 +1338,5 @@
-				now_pressed = ev.time.tv_usec + ev.time.tv_sec * 1000000ULL;
+#if defined(__USE_TIME_BITS64) && (__BITS_PER_LONG == 32)
+				now_pressed = ev.__usec + ev.__sec * 1000000ULL;
+#else
+				now_pressed = ev.time.tv_usec + ev.time.tv_sec * 1000000ULL;
+#endif
